{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Texture that offsets the tangent map for anisotropy calculations and optionally controls the anisotropy effect (if an alpha channel is present). The flowmap texture is expected to be a derivative map, with the red channel representing distortion on the X axis and green channel representing distortion on the Y axis. Values below 0.5 will result in negative distortion, whereas values above 0.5 will result in positive distortion."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anisotropyFlowmap","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Texture2D","text":"Texture2D","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot9Texture2DC"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If present, the texture’s alpha channel will be used to multiply the strength of the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/anisotropy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" effect. Fully opaque pixels will keep the anisotropy effect’s original strength while fully transparent pixels will disable the anisotropy effect entirely. The flowmap texture’s blue channel is ignored."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/BaseMaterial3D\/anisotropyFlowmap","interfaceLangua